---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { business as b } from '../data/site';
---
<Base
  title="The Studio: A Marsh-View Recording Sanctuary in St. Augustine | The Fish Tank"
  description="An elevated recording studio down a private drive overlooking the St. Augustine marsh, with a huge deck, an SSL Origin console and a FLEA U47. A sanctuary for artists since 2002."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'The Studio', path: '/studio/' }]}
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="About · The sanctuary" title="Where the music meets <em>the marsh.</em>"
    lede={`Down a private drive, up above the St. Augustine marsh, there’s a place where the outside world falls away. The tubes are warm, the coffee’s on and the view goes on for miles. Since ${b.founded}, The Fish Tank has been a sanctuary for artists to collaborate, create and reconnect with both their music and the calm of nature.`} />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="gallery">
        <div class="photo photo--wide g1">The deck at golden hour · marsh view (to shoot)</div>
        <div class="photo g2">Control room · SSL Origin (to shoot)</div>
        <div class="photo g3">Vocal mic · FLEA U47 (to shoot)</div>
        <div class="photo g4">Bass & guitar wall (to shoot)</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="wrap grid split">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>A sanctuary, <em>not a booking room.</em></h2>
        <p>Most studios are windowless boxes in a strip of warehouses. The Fish Tank sits in a beautiful elevated space with a world-class view of the St. Augustine marsh: herons gliding over the grass, the tide breathing in and out, and sunsets that turn the whole sky amber.</p>
        <p>Step out between takes onto the massive deck and let the song settle. Clear your head, talk through the bridge, or just listen to the marsh. Then walk back in and nail it. This is where artists come to find their connection again, to each other, to their music and to the quiet of the natural world.</p>

        <h2>Built for <em>making records.</em></h2>
        <p>Lu designed The Fish Tank to be part of the creative process. Songs get written on that couch. Vocals get coached into something fearless. Records get tracked, mixed and mastered without ever leaving the property.</p>
        <p>The beating heart of the control room is an <strong>SSL Origin</strong> console feeding <strong>Pro Tools HD</strong>, flanked by a rack of character from Shadow Hills, Elysia, API, Empirical Labs and A-Designs. Step up to the mic and you’re singing into a <strong>FLEA U47 Next</strong>, the modern heir to the most legendary vocal mic ever built, with Royer and AEA ribbons standing by for velvet-smooth guitars and room sound. Personal monitor mixes let a five-piece band track together, live and loud.</p>
        <p>Then there’s the candy store: a wall of basses (P-Bass, StingRay fretless, Dingwall, Zon and a 6-string), guitars from Collings, PRS and Taylor, an upright, a Dobro, a banjotar and a Medicine Man kit waiting to be hit.</p>
        <p><a href="/gear/">Full gear list →</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Visit</p>
        <h3>{b.street}<br />{b.city}, {b.region} {b.postal}</h3>
        <p>Private drive · marsh-view deck · sessions by appointment</p>
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Book a session →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .gallery { display: grid; gap: 1rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  .g1 { grid-column: 1 / -1; aspect-ratio: 21/9; }
  .g2, .g3, .g4 { aspect-ratio: 4/5; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .gallery { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .g1 { aspect-ratio: 16/10; } }
</style>
